      "content": "Absolutely, you can monitor the wound for a few days. If it starts to swell, becomes red, or you notice any pus, then you should consider getting a tetanus shot. But for now, keep it clean and apply some antibiotic ointment to prevent infection. And remember, I'm here to help you, so don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions. Just be sure to keep an eye on it and take care of yourself.",
